    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green. The audit log confirms the new behavior working end-to-end: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` for a registration date of `2026-08-17` \u2014 August 2026 falls in fiscal year 2027 (starting 1 July 2026), so the year segment is now `M27` rather than the old calendar-based `M26`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 the Australian convention consistent with the app's NSW/VIC/QLD locale).\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `mapper/FiscalYear.java`: `yearOf(date)` returns the fiscal year (month \u2265 July \u2192 year+1, else year); `of(date)` formats it as `FY<YY>`, returning `null` when the date is absent.\n\n**`fiscalYear` field** (`FY<YY>`, derived at read time from the business-day-adjusted registration date):\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` property to the Owner schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `@Mapping` expression `FiscalYear.of(owner.getRegistrationDate())` and imported the helper.\n\n**Membership identifier year segment** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.assignMembershipNumber`): now uses `FiscalYear.yearOf(...)` instead of the calendar year. Updated the openapi description/example.\n\n**Tenure** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`): `TENURE_LEVEL_THRESHOLD_DAYS = 365` \u2192 `TENURE_LEVEL_THRESHOLD_FISCAL_YEARS = 1`, and `tenureDays` \u2192 `tenureFiscalYears`, counting elapsed fiscal years rather than 365-day windows. As before, a newly created owner has zero tenure, so the level-4 tenure bonus never applies on create \u2014 behavior preserved, unit changed. Updated the `membershipPoints` description accordingly.\n\nNull handling is preserved throughout: seed owners without a `registrationDate` simply omit `fiscalYear` (same pattern as `ageBand`).",
